    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Known gaps",
      "id": 29,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 92
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "- **Guest OS boot and application start times**: not visible from outside. The disk read burst after a start is a good proxy (it settles in about 90-120 s), but it needs each desktop's start time as a metric to be drawn here.\n- **Viewer latency and disconnections**: client RTT and who ends a session need structured proxy logs with timers.\n- **Native SPICE and RDP clients**: Faro only sees the browser; these have to be measured on the server side.\n- **Quality by site**: grouping by each site's public (NAT) address needs a per-connection metric.\n- **Hypervisor CPU and I/O pressure (PSI)**: not exported yet."
      }
    }
